{
  "chapter.2465986E2653D08D.title": "02 • Ad Astra: From Earth to Glacio",
  "task.7476A524D271277C.title": "I read and understood this guide",
  "quest.0427FC81E857F60B.title": "Start here: Ad Astra",
  "quest.0427FC81E857F60B.quest_subtitle": "Guide and tips",
  "quest.0427FC81E857F60B.quest_desc": [
    "&6&lWHY&r",
    "Ad Astra adds rockets, planets and space infrastructure. Progression combines manufacturing with life support: each new destination offers resources for the next tier, but travel also requires a way to breathe and return.",
    "",
    "&a&lDO&r",
    "Your route: steel workshop -> rocket and fuel -> suit and oxygen -> Moon and Desh -> Mars and Ostrum -> hot worlds and Calorite -> Glacio and an orbital base.",
    "",
    "&e&lTIP&r",
    "Read the next guide card before building. This chapter teaches working setups; it does not replace JEI recipes or the mod's own manual."
  ],
  "task.2BCC9C185A201064.title": "I read and understood this guide",
  "quest.43205FAABE71A19D.title": "How to use this guide",
  "quest.43205FAABE71A19D.quest_subtitle": "Guide and tips",
  "quest.43205FAABE71A19D.quest_desc": [
    "&6&lWHY&r",
    "Arrows suggest a learning order. Item tasks check what you carry; a checkmark is your own confirmation of a practical step. Neither is proof that an entire machine or colony works.",
    "",
    "&a&lDO&r",
    "Open a quest, read Why / Do / Tip, then click its item to inspect it in JEI. R shows recipes and U shows uses with the default bindings. Read ahead, complete the described experiment, and only then tick practical tasks. Items are not consumed.",
    "",
    "&e&lTIP&r",
    "Use JEI for this pack's quantities and substitutions. Pick a small test area and keep outputs visible. Existing equipment can count; briefly pick it up only when safe. Troubleshooting and a final project are at the end."
  ],
  "quest.5E8B76ADCE0FFF3C.title": "Your flight manual",
  "quest.5E8B76ADCE0FFF3C.quest_subtitle": "Item milestone",
  "quest.5E8B76ADCE0FFF3C.quest_desc": [
    "&6&lWHY&r",
    "The Astrodux explains the installed version's machines and environmental rules. It is especially useful when a recipe differs from an older video.",
    "",
    "&a&lDO&r",
    "Craft and open the Astrodux. Read The First Launch, then bookmark the oxygen and return-trip pages. Use JEI for the pack's actual machine and rocket recipes.",
    "",
    "&e&lTIP&r",
    "This chapter follows the bundled 1.16.26 guide. Suit upgrades and oxygen systems are not optional just because another mod gives you strong armor."
  ],
  "task.4D00AE36EC335238.title": "I completed the practical steps",
  "quest.602ABAC97C81CCCB.title": "Power the workshop",
  "quest.602ABAC97C81CCCB.quest_subtitle": "Practical checklist",
  "quest.602ABAC97C81CCCB.quest_desc": [
    "&6&lWHY&r",
    "Machines need FE before you can make plates, process fuel or load oxygen. A small independent workshop is easy to troubleshoot.",
    "",
    "&a&lDO&r",
    "Supply FE using the Coal Generator or an existing compatible source. Connect one machine, inspect its energy bar and run a simple process before adding more loads.",
    "",
    "&e&lTIP&r",
    "Check machine sides and redstone settings when a cable touches a machine but no energy enters."
  ],
  "quest.371075639BD2B993.title": "Steel for spacecraft",
  "quest.371075639BD2B993.quest_subtitle": "Item milestone",
  "quest.371075639BD2B993.quest_desc": [
    "&6&lWHY&r",
    "Steel is a key structural material for your first space equipment. Its processing route is determined by this pack's recipes.",
    "",
    "&a&lDO&r",
    "Inspect Steel Ingot in JEI and make a small batch using an available route. Check the Etrionic Blast Furnace recipe and uses if you want an Ad Astra-focused workshop.",
    "",
    "&e&lTIP&r",
    "Do not guess that every steel tag works in every rocket part. Check the actual ingredient slots before making a large batch."
  ],
  "task.2771AE0F5E8DD8A5.title": "I completed the practical steps",
  "quest.46BB06D66C3C9942.title": "Make plates",
  "quest.46BB06D66C3C9942.quest_subtitle": "Practical checklist",
  "quest.46BB06D66C3C9942.quest_desc": [
    "&6&lWHY&r",
    "The Compressor turns materials into components for machines and rockets.",
    "",
    "&a&lDO&r",
    "Power the Compressor, insert a recipe-compatible ingot and collect a plate. Compare its uses in JEI and reserve enough material for the engine, tanks and rocket body.",
    "",
    "&e&lTIP&r",
    "Process a small batch first. Rocket assembly needs several distinct components, not just a pile of plates."
  ],
  "task.4F1C9CDABAB6B6FB.title": "I completed the practical steps",
  "quest.7E98C22B11EC4896.title": "Refine rocket fuel",
  "quest.7E98C22B11EC4896.quest_subtitle": "Practical checklist",
  "quest.7E98C22B11EC4896.quest_desc": [
    "&6&lWHY&r",
    "Oil is a feedstock; rockets need a supported fuel. The refinery converts collected oil into usable fuel.",
    "",
    "&a&lDO&r",
    "Find oil using the Astrodux guidance, collect it, and run a powered Fuel Refinery. Store the result in clearly separated containers. Prepare enough for both departure and return.",
    "",
    "&e&lTIP&r",
    "Do not mix oil, oxygen and fuel plumbing. Read the fluid name on the tank before filling the rocket."
  ],
  "task.5B26CB233F169A09.title": "I completed the practical steps",
  "quest.35B4A2C4984E736C.title": "Rocket assembly bench",
  "quest.35B4A2C4984E736C.quest_subtitle": "Practical checklist",
  "quest.35B4A2C4984E736C.quest_desc": [
    "&6&lWHY&r",
    "Rockets are assembled at the NASA Workbench using a complete set of parts.",
    "",
    "&a&lDO&r",
    "Craft the workbench and open the Tier 1 recipe. Make its required cone, plates, fins, tanks and engine, then assemble the rocket.",
    "",
    "&e&lTIP&r",
    "Use the recipe for your selected tier. Higher-tier engines and tanks are not automatically interchangeable."
  ],
  "task.25F0456FD23592E8.title": "I completed the practical steps",
  "quest.03EBF6343E93AED7.title": "Launch pad and rocket",
  "quest.03EBF6343E93AED7.quest_subtitle": "Practical checklist",
  "quest.03EBF6343E93AED7.quest_desc": [
    "&6&lWHY&r",
    "The rocket needs its launch pad and fuel, not just an open patch of ground.",
    "",
    "&a&lDO&r",
    "Build a Launch Pad, place the Tier 1 Rocket at its center and open its inventory. Fuel it and inspect its storage. Keep the launch area clear above and around the craft.",
    "",
    "&e&lTIP&r",
    "Avoid powering the launch pad accidentally: its redstone behavior can launch a fueled rocket."
  ],
  "task.30335D77925F0DED.title": "I completed the practical steps",
  "quest.1772CF3D1B830C75.title": "A complete space suit",
  "quest.1772CF3D1B830C75.quest_subtitle": "Practical checklist",
  "quest.1772CF3D1B830C75.quest_desc": [
    "&6&lWHY&r",
    "The chestpiece stores oxygen, but a partial outfit is not a complete life-support solution.",
    "",
    "&a&lDO&r",
    "Craft the helmet, chestpiece, pants and boots. Equip the full set and inspect the oxygen readout. Check each piece rather than assuming your normal combat armor covers the same hazards.",
    "",
    "&e&lTIP&r",
    "Any alternative suit integration must be configured and tested on Earth first. Keep the Ad Astra suit as your known working baseline."
  ],
  "task.13C00520EF55E642.title": "I completed the practical steps",
  "quest.33D8C2874025A9C2.title": "Load oxygen",
  "quest.33D8C2874025A9C2.quest_subtitle": "Practical checklist",
  "quest.33D8C2874025A9C2.quest_desc": [
    "&6&lWHY&r",
    "Oxygen is a consumable travel resource. Empty tanks and an unfilled chestpiece will not protect you.",
    "",
    "&a&lDO&r",
    "Power the Oxygen Loader and provide water as described in the Astrodux. Fill the suit and spare tanks through its interface. Confirm that the stored oxygen values increase.",
    "",
    "&e&lTIP&r",
    "Hold right-click with a filled Oxygen Tank to distribute oxygen to compatible carried items, prioritizing armor."
  ],
  "task.370CCEFA81B6C73D.title": "I read and understood this guide",
  "quest.370DC82F574E180A.title": "Preflight: come home",
  "quest.370DC82F574E180A.quest_subtitle": "Guide and tips",
  "quest.370DC82F574E180A.quest_desc": [
    "&6&lWHY&r",
    "A successful launch includes landing, survival and a return trip. Your spare fuel should stay separate from your exploration budget.",
    "",
    "&a&lDO&r",
    "Pack a return Launch Pad and three buckets of ordinary fuel, or the verified equivalent for your chosen fuel. Bring full spare oxygen tanks, food, tools, solid blocks and soul torches/glowstone. Equip and fill the full suit before entering the rocket.",
    "",
    "&e&lTIP&r",
    "The bundled guide specifies three ordinary fuel buckets for the return. Check the actual rocket gauge; do not spend your return reserve exploring."
  ],
  "task.5625958D90C6A500.title": "I completed the practical steps",
  "quest.575B1E148392A4AA.title": "First Moon landing",
  "quest.575B1E148392A4AA.quest_subtitle": "Practical checklist",
  "quest.575B1E148392A4AA.quest_desc": [
    "&6&lWHY&r",
    "The Moon provides Desh for the next tier. Your first visit should establish a return point before a long mining expedition.",
    "",
    "&a&lDO&r",
    "Enter the rocket, use your jump key to launch, and choose the Moon. After landing, sneak-right-click the lander to retrieve your rocket and cargo. Secure the site and check oxygen before leaving.",
    "",
    "&e&lTIP&r",
    "Ordinary torches and exposed crops are unsuitable for the Moon. Keep your suit equipped until a shelter is demonstrably safe."
  ],
  "task.24BBC45917AE82CE.title": "I completed the practical steps",
  "quest.216D2FCAB60B42A8.title": "Bring back Desh",
  "quest.216D2FCAB60B42A8.quest_subtitle": "Practical checklist",
  "quest.216D2FCAB60B42A8.quest_desc": [
    "&6&lWHY&r",
    "Desh unlocks better infrastructure and the Tier 2 rocket. Bringing a modest sample home proves the whole travel loop works.",
    "",
    "&a&lDO&r",
    "Mine Desh, process it with a recipe shown in JEI, then make a return trip using your reserved rocket, pad and fuel.",
    "",
    "&e&lTIP&r",
    "Mark your landing site. A waypoint is navigation help, not a substitute for oxygen or a working return vehicle."
  ],
  "task.2C33E78F8A36D087.title": "I completed the practical steps",
  "quest.1C879BB1FC86D78E.title": "Build a breathable room",
  "quest.1C879BB1FC86D78E.quest_subtitle": "Practical checklist",
  "quest.1C879BB1FC86D78E.quest_desc": [
    "&6&lWHY&r",
    "An Oxygen Distributor makes a sealed room habitable when it has water and power. It is a base system, unlike the loader used for suit supplies.",
    "",
    "&a&lDO&r",
    "Build a small sealed room. Connect a powered Water Pump over an infinite source to the distributor, power both machines, and use the distributor's Show function to verify coverage and leaks.",
    "",
    "&e&lTIP&r",
    "Cables and ordinary pipes may leave openings. Use the appropriate ducts through walls and check the room before removing your suit."
  ],
  "task.6B1E5D4AC612F258.title": "I completed the practical steps",
  "quest.7BE7E6D3362B889B.title": "Measure the environment",
  "quest.7BE7E6D3362B889B.quest_subtitle": "Practical checklist",
  "quest.7BE7E6D3362B889B.quest_desc": [
    "&6&lWHY&r",
    "Habitability involves oxygen, temperature and gravity. A room that looks enclosed may still be unsafe.",
    "",
    "&a&lDO&r",
    "Use the Ti-69 to inspect local conditions. Add an Oxygen Sensor if you want a redstone status indicator; inspect its detection mode and compare the reading inside and outside the shelter.",
    "",
    "&e&lTIP&r",
    "Use airlocks and confirm conditions after modifying walls. Treat a newly opened doorway as a reason to recheck life support."
  ],
  "task.4E98708C3FECCB03.title": "I completed the practical steps",
  "quest.15225DADFC0914E0.title": "Tier 2: Mars",
  "quest.15225DADFC0914E0.quest_subtitle": "Practical checklist",
  "quest.15225DADFC0914E0.quest_desc": [
    "&6&lWHY&r",
    "Mars is the next resource step after the Moon. Desh components enable the rocket needed to reach it.",
    "",
    "&a&lDO&r",
    "Assemble a Tier 2 Rocket using the NASA Workbench recipe. Repeat preflight checks, travel to Mars and obtain Ostrum for the next stage.",
    "",
    "&e&lTIP&r",
    "Reuse your checklist on every trip. A better rocket does not automatically fill your suit or carry spare fuel."
  ],
  "task.39E20508B38F6BAA.title": "I completed the practical steps",
  "quest.112081DBB9670E96.title": "Improve fuel and power",
  "quest.112081DBB9670E96.quest_subtitle": "Practical checklist",
  "quest.112081DBB9670E96.quest_desc": [
    "&6&lWHY&r",
    "Cryo Fuel can make repeated flights more efficient, while solar generation helps support remote installations.",
    "",
    "&a&lDO&r",
    "Inspect Cryo Freezer recipes for ice-related inputs and produce a batch. Check how much your rocket needs, then retain a separate return supply. Inspect Solar Panel output on your chosen world.",
    "",
    "&e&lTIP&r",
    "Generation varies with location and atmosphere. Size energy storage for periods when your source cannot support the base."
  ],
  "quest.29B3EBF9795A73D6.title": "Protect against heat",
  "quest.29B3EBF9795A73D6.quest_subtitle": "Item milestone",
  "quest.29B3EBF9795A73D6.quest_desc": [
    "&6&lWHY&r",
    "Hot planets require equipment beyond the basic space suit. Their resources should not be pursued with an untested outfit.",
    "",
    "&a&lDO&r",
    "Use Ostrum progression to obtain the upgraded space equipment shown in the Astrodux. Complete and fill the full upgraded set before planning a hot-world landing.",
    "",
    "&e&lTIP&r",
    "A netherite chestplate from another mod is not the Netherite Space Suit. Verify the exact item names and full outfit."
  ],
  "task.084F5FA9F06A65BA.title": "I completed the practical steps",
  "quest.4284386F90782B0B.title": "Tier 3 and Calorite",
  "quest.4284386F90782B0B.quest_subtitle": "Practical checklist",
  "quest.4284386F90782B0B.quest_desc": [
    "&6&lWHY&r",
    "The next rocket tier reaches the hot worlds where Calorite supports late spacecraft and equipment.",
    "",
    "&a&lDO&r",
    "Assemble a Tier 3 Rocket, verify your heat-capable suit, oxygen and return kit, then select the intended hot-world destination. Bring back Calorite and inspect its uses.",
    "",
    "&e&lTIP&r",
    "Do not use a test of armor protection as your first survival experiment on Venus. Confirm the Astrodux requirements before departure."
  ],
  "task.6345453A4CEF36D1.title": "I completed the practical steps",
  "quest.337557221E144235.title": "Tier 4: Glacio",
  "quest.337557221E144235.quest_subtitle": "Practical checklist",
  "quest.337557221E144235.quest_desc": [
    "&6&lWHY&r",
    "Calorite enables travel beyond the initial solar system and completes the core rocket-tier progression.",
    "",
    "&a&lDO&r",
    "Build the Tier 4 Rocket, use the planet screen to travel toward Glacio, and establish a marked landing site. Measure local conditions rather than carrying assumptions over from the Moon.",
    "",
    "&e&lTIP&r",
    "Bring a return kit even for a world with breathable oxygen. Breathable air does not create fuel or a landing pad for you."
  ],
  "task.7CB8C32D0EA6A9AA.title": "I read and understood this guide",
  "quest.70A829E91698D799.title": "An orbital outpost",
  "quest.70A829E91698D799.quest_subtitle": "Guide and tips",
  "quest.70A829E91698D799.quest_desc": [
    "&6&lWHY&r",
    "A space station is a platform for a permanent orbital base, with different movement and life-support needs from a planet.",
    "",
    "&a&lDO&r",
    "Inspect the station construction requirements in the planet screen. Create a station when supplied, secure walkways, then establish power and verified oxygen coverage before expanding.",
    "",
    "&e&lTIP&r",
    "In low or zero gravity, control your momentum and keep solid boundaries nearby. A Gravity Normalizer is optional infrastructure with its own power cost."
  ],
  "task.0EF717AD00C74897.title": "I completed the practical steps",
  "quest.637DED48D606987A.title": "Project: repeatable expedition",
  "quest.637DED48D606987A.quest_subtitle": "Practical checklist",
  "quest.637DED48D606987A.quest_desc": [
    "&6&lWHY&r",
    "The real milestone is a trip you can repeat without rebuilding your preparation process every time.",
    "",
    "&a&lDO&r",
    "Create a labeled launch-supplies chest, maintain fuel and oxygen reserves, and complete an outbound-and-return trip. Leave one small outpost with a documented power and life-support arrangement.",
    "",
    "&e&lTIP&r",
    "If something fails, check fuel, suit oxygen, environmental protection, machine power, water supply and sealing separately."
  ]
}
